cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Cross-Domain Robustness Synthesis: Does a Single Retention Metric Generalise?"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Moharampudi
    given-names: Akshith
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3177-8492"
repository-code: "https://github.com/akshith2001/cross-domain-robustness-synthesis"
abstract: >-
  A synthesis testing whether a single robustness-retention ratio can
  meaningfully compare "degradation under stress" across three
  independently evaluated machine-learning research projects. TrustLens
  and Hospitality inputs come from released result documents; the GHG
  ratio is deterministically re-derived from released code and data. An
  equally defensible alternative within-domain comparison
  widens the observed cross-domain range by more than 4x and flips at
  least one project's ranking from most to least robust.
keywords:
  - trustworthy AI
  - robustness evaluation
  - cross-domain generalisation
  - responsible AI
  - evaluation methodology
  - research synthesis
